#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0369 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "Expansion: ^(.+)DTF$ matches ADTF (root 'A'); ^(.+)DT$ matches ADT (root 'A'); ^(.+)DTM$ matches ADTM (root 'A'). All three seed the same tuple -> ONE expansion not empty(ADTF) and empty(ADT) and empty(ADTM). All three columns are declared, so the post-expansion arm-1 guards var_exists(ADT)/var_exists(ADTM) are satisfied and the record-level Check fires on row 1."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ADTF=D
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ADTF    type=Char
col ADT     type=Num
col ADTM    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | D | |
